A '''racer''' was [[pilot]]ed by [[Jace Rucklin]]. In an effort to save weight and make the [[Starship|ship]] faster, all systems deemed "extraneous," including the [[Ejector seat|ejection seat]] [[parachute]], were removed from it. It was destroyed after Rucklin, in an attempt to gain any advantage, added stolen [[Coaxium|hyperfuel]] to the ship without knowing the safe amount to use. The ship was consequently turned into a "flying bomb," and exploded after a short time. Rucklin was only saved due to the daring efforts of [[Kazuda Xiono]], who rescued him with the ejection seat at great danger to his own life. Rucklin was not grateful, as he had sunk all his savings into the ship, and ignored his own fault in the incident to blame Xiono, vowing to get him back for the loss of the racer.<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" />

{{Ship-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Rucklin's racer first appeared in "[[Fuel for the Fire]],"<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" /> the fourth episode of the [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|first season]] of the ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'' animated television series which premiered on [[October 21]], [[2018]].<ref name="Disney Press">{{DisneyPress|wdtv=1|url=disneychannel/shows/star-wars-resistance/episodes|text=Star Wars Resistance}}</ref> The ship was identified as "Rucklin's new racer" in the episode.<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" />

